# Chaos runtime artifacts (not source). The broader chaos* pattern that
# previously lived here also blocked new source files like chaos_binding_test.go.
chaos-runs/
screen-traces/
chaos-hints.json
chaos-workflow*.json
chaos-output*.json
/chaos*.log

# Connection profiles are per-deployment runtime state, written by the app at
# its base directory — configuration for an install, not source.
/profiles.json
/profiles.json.tmp

# The bind-mounted data folder from docker-compose.yml: accounts, tokens, the
# audit trail and everyone's saved work.
/data/

# A local convenience symlink (s3270 -> s3270-linux-amd64) so a Linux
# checkout can run `go run ./cmd/3270Web` directly: the resolver looks for
# s3270-bin/s3270, while the repo ships the binary under its platform name.
# A symlink must not be committed — a Windows checkout would materialise it
# as a plain text file and the resolver would try to execute that.
/s3270-bin/s3270
